<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Ottto third-party Rust licenses</title>
<style>
body { max-width: 75ch; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; font-family: sans-serif; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Ottto third-party Rust licenses</h1>
<p>License notices for the third-party Rust crates in the Apple Silicon
<code>ottto</code> CLI and <code>ottto-service</code> daemon, including transitive
dependencies, build scripts and procedural macros. Ottto's own code is covered by
the accompanying LICENSE and NOTICE files.</p>
<p>Generated with cargo-about 0.9.2 from Cargo.lock for aarch64-apple-darwin.
Where a crate offers a choice of licenses, the license it is listed under is the
one Ottto uses. objc2-core-foundation and objc2-core-services are offered under
Zlib, Apache-2.0 or MIT; Ottto uses them under Apache-2.0.</p>
{{#each licenses}}
<section data-license="{{id}}">
<h2>{{name}} ({{id}})</h2>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
<li data-crate="{{crate.name}}" data-version="{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
